---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | wrongfulterminationcalc.com"
  description="Privacy policy for wrongfulterminationcalc.com. Learn how we collect, use, and share information, including the case-review form."
>

  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated: July 2026</em></p>

  <p>
    WrongfulTerminationCalc ("we," "us," or "our") is operated by The Click Lab Agency LLC and runs wrongfulterminationcalc.com (the "Site"). This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and protect information about visitors to our Site.
  </p>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Calculator inputs:</strong> When you use our settlement calculator, the values you enter (salary, years employed, claim type, state, contract status) are processed entirely in your browser using JavaScript. We do not transmit, store, or have access to any values you enter into the calculator. Simply browsing the calculator and guides never requires you to provide personal information.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Case-review form:</strong> If you choose to submit the "Wrongful Termination" case-review form on the homepage, we collect your name, phone number, email address, the case details you provide, and a timestamp of your consent. This is separate from using the calculator and is entirely optional &mdash; see "The Case-Review Form and Attorney Sharing" below for what happens to this information.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Usage data:</strong> Like most websites, we automatically collect certain technical information when you visit: your IP address, browser type, device type, operating system, referring URL, pages visited, and time spent on pages. This data is collected through analytics software (Google Analytics) and is used to understand how visitors use the Site and to improve our content.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Cookies:</strong> We use cookies for analytics and advertising purposes. Google Analytics sets cookies to track visits and usage patterns. Google AdSense sets cookies to serve relevant advertisements. You can control cookies through your browser settings.
  </p>

  <h2>The Case-Review Form and Attorney Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    If you submit the case-review form, your name, phone number, email address, and case details are shared with one or more attorneys or their agents licensed to practice in your jurisdiction, so they can evaluate your situation and contact you about it. The Click Lab Agency LLC, which operates wrongfulterminationcalc.com, is not a law firm, does not provide legal advice, and does not vet, endorse, or guarantee the attorneys in this network. Submitting the form does not create an attorney-client relationship with The Click Lab Agency LLC or with any attorney until and unless that attorney separately agrees to represent you. The Click Lab Agency LLC may be compensated for these referrals.
  </p>
  <p>
    By submitting the form, you separately consent to be contacted by phone, text, and email &mdash; including by automated dialing technology &mdash; by The Click Lab Agency LLC and the attorneys or agents your information is shared with. That consent is not required to use any other part of this Site, and you can decline it by not submitting the form.
  </p>

  <h2>Google AdSense</h2>
  <p>
    We use Google AdSense to display advertising on the Site. Google AdSense uses cookies and web beacons to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website and other sites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visit to our site and/or other sites on the Internet. You may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Ads Settings</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use Google Analytics 4 (measurement ID G-VRDRZSY4XV) to understand how visitors interact with our Site. Google Analytics collects information such as how often users visit the Site, what pages they visit, and what other sites they used prior to coming to our Site. We use this information to improve the Site. Google Analytics collects only the IP address assigned to you on the date you visit the Site, not your name or other identifying information. We do not combine the information collected through Google Analytics with personally identifiable information. For information on how Google Analytics uses data, visit <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To operate and improve the Site and its content</li>
    <li>To understand how visitors use the Site</li>
    <li>To display relevant advertising through Google AdSense</li>
    <li>To respond to communications you send us</li>
    <li>If you submit the case-review form, to share your information with attorneys or their agents so they can evaluate and contact you about your case, as described above</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Information Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell, rent, or share your personal information with third parties for marketing purposes unrelated to what you asked for. If you submit the case-review form, we share your name, phone number, email address, and case details with attorneys or their agents as described above &mdash; that sharing happens only if you take that specific, optional action. We may share aggregated, non-personally identifiable information with analytics partners. We may share information when required by law, subpoena, or other legal process.
  </p>

  <h2>Opting Out</h2>
  <p>
    The simplest opt-out is not to submit the case-review form &mdash; every other part of the Site (the calculator and guides) is fully usable without providing any personal information. If you already submitted the form and want your information removed or want to withdraw consent to be contacted, email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a> with the subject line <code>[OPT-OUT]</code>, or visit <a href="https://theclicklab.agency/optout">theclicklab.agency/optout</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Data Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We retain analytics data in aggregated, anonymized form. Case-review form submissions and email correspondence are retained only as long as needed to fulfill the referral or respond to your message, plus a reasonable period afterward for record-keeping, unless you request deletion sooner.
  </p>

  <h2>Your Rights (CCPA/CPRA and GDPR)</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have rights to access, correct, or delete personal information we hold about you, and to opt out of certain processing.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>California residents:</strong> sharing your information with attorneys for compensation, as described above, may be considered a "sale" or "share" of personal information under the CCPA/CPRA. You have the right to opt out of this at any time using the channels in the "Opting Out" section above. Anonymous browsing of the calculator and guides alone is never sold or shared, because it doesn't involve any personal information.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>EU/UK residents:</strong> the legal basis for processing the information you submit through the case-review form is your consent, which you may withdraw at any time using the same channels.
  </p>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these rights, contact us at hey@theclicklab.agency.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    The Site is not directed to children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will post any changes on this page with an updated date. Continued use of the Site after changes are posted constitutes your acceptance of the revised policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this Privacy Policy? Contact us at <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>.
  </p>

</BaseLayout>
